# example-tickets — one work item, start to finish

This file is an example template. Copy it into your config's `templates/skills/`, rename it and write
your own process; the tokens below are the ones the engine fills from `manifest.yaml`.

## 1 · Find the item

```bash
{{.Tickets.CLI}} --config {{.Tickets.Config}} list "{{.Tickets.TasksDB}}"{{.Tickets.TaskFilter}} --limit 20
{{.Tickets.CLI}} --config {{.Tickets.Config}} list "{{.Tickets.BugsDB}}"{{.Tickets.BugFilter}} --limit 20
```

Refs look like `{{.Tickets.RefScheme.Task}}` / `{{.Tickets.RefScheme.Bug}}`. Take the top item of
{{.Tickets.States.Todo}} by priority ({{.Tickets.PriorityChain}}); its dependencies are written as
`{{.Tickets.DependsOn}}`. Fields worth reading besides the description: `{{.Tickets.Space}}/MR`
(merge request URL){{if .Tickets.ExtraFields}}, {{.Tickets.ExtraFields}}{{end}}.

Move it to {{.Tickets.States.InProgress}} before writing code; to {{.Tickets.States.InReview}} when
the gates are green.

